<title>USA: Allied Healthcare St. Louis workers strike.</title>
<headline>Allied Healthcare St. Louis workers strike.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allied Healthcare Products Inc, a respiratory therapy equipment maker, said Monday its St. Louis shop employees represented by the Machinist Union initiated a work stoppage Sunday morning.</p>
<p>The work stoppage affects 277 workers at the company's St. Louis facility, the company said. The company said its operations in Oakland, California; Riverside, California; Toledo, Ohio; and Stuyvesant Falls, New York are not affected by this work stoppage.</p>
<p>The company said it it using salaried personnel and outside sources in efforts to service customers.</p>
<p>Allied Healthcare Products shares fell 3/8 to 5-3/4 Monday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
